the home of the University of Idaho has  been shaken up by the deaths of four  students and people there still know  very little about how or why the victims  were killed the bodies of three women  and one man all 21 or under were found  together over the weekend police say  that they have released all the  information that they can at this time  without jeopardizing their investigation  but they insist there is no wider threat  to the public yet there have still been  no arrest and there are still a lot of  unanswered questions in this case  Jonathan Vigliotti has been following  this story  police in the city of Moscow say the  four University of Idaho students who  were killed in this home across the  street from campus Sunday were victims  of a targeted attack investigators  believe a quote edged weapon such as a  knife was used although no weapon was  recovered from the scene this is a  pretty dramatic situation for our Campus  Community the victims appeared to have  been close friends on the same day they  were killed Kaylee gonsalves posted this  picture showing all four students  smiling while posing together one lucky  girl to be surrounded by these people  every day she wrote Zanna kernodle  posted this loving message about Ethan  Chapin saying life is so much better  with you in it this morning their  families are grieving their loss zanna's  sister Jasmine kernodle telling CBS News  Zanna was so positive funny and was  loved by everyone who met her my family  and I are at a lot of words confused and  anxiously waiting for updates on the  investigation the murders were called a  crime of passion by the mayor but police  have not offered a potential motive for  a suspect well there was a lot of blood  when asked Tuesday about the possibility  of a murder-suicide the County coroner  was adamant someone else was responsible  now there are four homicides authorities  say there is no imminent threat to the  community at large a lot of people left  last night but many front-end students  have decided to go on Thanksgiving break  a week early my mom has called me every  single hour they want me to come home if  I don't feel safe for CBS mornings I'm  Jonathan Vigliotti  it's very troubling authorities clearly  know something but it's hard to ask  people to be patient when you have four  people dead and no one can understand  that parent calling four times a day  every hour yeah you're right about that  yeah
 

